      "tvm_method_id": 123660,
      "name": "dnsresolve",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "subdomain",
          "ty_idx": 2
        },
        {
          "name": "category",
          "ty_idx": 17
        }
      ],
      "return_ty_idx": 23,
      "description": "TEP-81. R8-1 — THE DELEGATING STUB. See the DnsConfig note above for why the\ncollection answers this at all.\n\n`.ton`'s collection consumes the top label and delegates to a PER-NAME item,\nwhich then answers the leftover \"\\0\" from its own storage. Ours cannot: our\nrecords live in one contract keyed on the bare label, not in the item. So this\nstub consumes ONLY the self-reference byte and hands the whole label onward —\n`\\0🚀🌙\\0` in, 8 bits consumed, `🚀🌙\\0` to the resolver, which is exactly the\nshape it already accepts (tests/R7RootAgnostic.spec.ts, \"THE BRIDGE\").\n\nA request must begin with `\\0`. TEP-81 requires that of every non-root\nresolver, and every real client does it — MyTonWallet prepends it in\n`dnsResolve()`, tonweb in `Dns.resolve()`. Without it we cannot report a\nprefix length that is both honest and non-zero, and 0 means LOOKUP FAILED."
    },
    {
      "tvm_method_id": 80906,
      "name": "handover_dns",
      "parameters": [],
      "return_ty_idx": 25,
      "description": "R8-6. `handover()` is the warning window R7-11 shipped, and a successor is\ntold to read it before accepting. It had no DNS field, so a staged zone\nredirect was invisible in exactly the view meant to surface staged changes.\nReturns (resolver, pendingResolver, pendingResolverAt) alongside it."
    },
    {
      "tvm_method_id": 78839,
      "name": "handover_content",
      "parameters": [],
      "return_ty_idx": 26,
      "description": "R9-5. The staged content change, readable for the full 48 hours before it\nlands. A timelock that nobody can observe buys no warning time — the same\nargument R7-11 made for `handover()` and R8-6 made for `handover_dns()`.\nReturns (pendingCollectionContent, pendingCommonContent, at); all null/0 when\nnothing is staged."
    },
    {
      "tvm_method_id": 75485,
      "name": "collection_resolver",
      "parameters": [],
      "return_ty_idx": 25,
      "description": "R8-1. The pointer, and anything staged against it. Lets an integrator confirm\nwhich record contract this zone currently delegates to, and see a pending\nmigration for the full 48 hours before it lands."
    },
    {
      "tvm_method_id": 85719,
      "name": "royalty_params",
      "parameters": [],
      "return_ty_idx": 27
    },
    {
      "tvm_method_id": 121605,
      "name": "handover_royalty",
      "parameters": [],
      "return_ty_idx": 28,
      "description": "R14-7. The staged royalty change, readable for the full 48 hours before it\nlands — same argument R7-11 made for `handover()`, R8-6 for `handover_dns()`\nand R9-5 for `handover_content()`. A timelock nobody can observe buys no\nwarning time, and this is the one field a seller's proceeds depend on at the\nmoment of sale. Returns (numerator, denominator, destination, at); all zero /\naddr_none when nothing is staged."
    },
